{"format_version": 1, "nodes": [{"snapshot_id": 0, "labels": ["__KGBuilder__", "Document"], "properties": {"path": "document.txt", "createdAt": "2026-08-30T09:39:32.127992+00:00", "document_type": "inline_text"}}, {"snapshot_id": 1, "labels": ["__KGBuilder__", "Chunk"], "properties": {"index": 0, "text": "DirectorSteven SpielbergStarsDennis WeaverJacqueline ScottEddie Firestone\n\n   \nImage 12: Natalie Portman in Black Swan (2010)   Rate\n\nMark as watched\n\nAn insecure ballerina finally gets the role she has always dreamed of, but as the pressures mount her line between reality and illusion starts to blur.\n\nDirectorDarren AronofskyStarsNatalie PortmanMila KunisVincent Cassel\n\n   \nImage 13: The Ring (2002)   Rate\n\nMark as watched [...] DirectorDarren AronofskyStarsSean GulletteMark MargolisBen Shenkman\n\n   \nImage 8: Michael Douglas in The Game (1997)   Rate\n\nMark as watched\n\nAn arrogant, isolated investment banker is targeted by an enigmatic entertainment company, plunging into an escalating, reality-bending conspiracy orchestrated by his estranged brother to shatter his emotional detachment.\n\nDirectorDavid FincherStarsMichael DouglasDeborah Kara UngerSean Penn\n\n   \nImage 9: Robert De Niro in Taxi Driver (1976)   Rate [...] DirectorDarren AronofskyStarsEllen BurstynJared LetoJennifer Connelly\n\n   \nImage 28: Willem Dafoe in Anamorph (2007)   Rate\n\nMark as watched\n\nA psychological thriller based on the concept of anamorphosis, a painting technique that manipulates the laws of perspective to create two competing images on a single canvas.\n\nDirectorHenry MillerStarsWillem DafoeScott SpeedmanDon Harvey\n\n   \nImage 29: Stellan Skarsg\u00e5rd and Melissa George in The Killing Gene (2007)   Rate\n\nMark as watched", "embedding": [-0.058927878737449646, -0.11523725092411041, -0.10131428390741348, -0.044382017105817795, 0.026567311957478523, 0.04519958794116974, 0.07302866876125336, 0.06535334140062332, 0.02373330667614937, 0.007579550612717867